# =====================================================================
# TRAMES monorepo
#
# The rule here is: anything that can be regenerated from a script in
# this repo does not belong in it. That is not a style preference —
# server/ alone holds 33 GB of OSM extract and routing graph, and the
# research data directory is another 583 MB of Census downloads.
# =====================================================================

# --- staging leftovers from the OsmAnd fork migration ----------------
/OsmAnd/
/resources/
/build-logs/

# --- routing server: downloaded and derived artifacts ----------------
# 18 GB continental extract, 14 GB prepared graph. Rebuild:
#   server/graphhopper/import.sh  (~82 min)
*.pbf
server/graphhopper/data/
server/graphhopper/graph-cache/
server/graphhopper/test-sandbox/
server/graphhopper/logs/
server/graphhopper/graphhopper-web-*.jar
graph-cache/

# Overpass responses and generated cone geometry (~55 MB).
# Rebuild: server/alpr/fetch-na-cones.sh + build_cones.py
region_cache*/
tile_cache/
**/custom_areas*/*.geojson
# study cone-set variants (vendor split, radius sweep) — server/alpr/build-variants.sh
server/alpr/variants/
# historical camera sets (fetch-history.sh) — regenerable from Overpass attic data
server/alpr/history/
# the map on the first of every month (~1 GB), and the quarterly dates routed in the second
# history graph (symlinks into it) — rebuilt in seconds by snapshot_from_versions.py from
# osm-history/node_versions.jsonl, then build_cones.py
server/alpr/history_monthly/
server/alpr/history2/
# OSM full-history dump (163 GB) and the validation extracts built from it
server/alpr/osm-history/
server/alpr/history-planet/

# --- research: downloaded inputs and heavy outputs -------------------
# 583 MB of Census Gazetteer / ACS / LODES. Rebuild: research/data/fetch.sh
# (the acquisition script itself is tracked — the paper tells readers to run it)
research/data/*
!research/data/fetch.sh
# the transparency-portal snapshot validate_coverage.py reads: a live API, so the dated copy is kept
!research/data/validation/
research/data/validation/*
!research/data/validation/transparency_portals_2026-09-24.json
# ~82 MB of route polylines. Regenerable, but only by re-running the
# full 7-hour experiment — kept out of git because it is over GitHub's
# comfortable file size, not because it is cheap.
research/out/**/routes.jsonl.gz
research/out/**/*.log
# siting analysis: the 11.5M-point road sample and the point-to-unit assignment caches (~2 GB).
# Rebuild with research/scripts/road_sample.py; siting.py re-creates the caches on its first run.
research/out/siting/*.npz
# the merged device map: ~520 MB of JSON holding every source record, rebuilt from the sources
# above by research/scripts/build_supermap.py (~4 min cold, ~80 s once its assignment caches
# exist), plus those caches. The report beside it (out/analysis_supermap.txt) IS committed.
research/out/supermap/*.json
research/out/supermap/*.json.gz
research/out/supermap/assign/
# the merged-map study's inputs, rebuilt by research/scripts/cones_from_supermap.py: the map's
# wedges (65 MB, as custom_areas*) and the registry readers it adds - a device-level list drawn
# from the registry, which, like the device map, the repository does not redistribute
research/out/merged/alpr_osm.geojson
research/out/merged/registry_discs.json
# US state boundary GeoJSON fetched by make_figures.py
research/paper/figures/us-states.json

# LaTeX build products (trames.pdf IS committed — see research/paper/)
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz

# --- Android / Gradle ------------------------------------------------
*.hprof
.gradle/
build/
client/build/
client/*/build/
local.properties
!client/ui-test-app/local.properties
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/
*.apk
*.aab
*.iml
captures/

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# --- editors / OS ----------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.swp

# generated by server/cameras/build_cameras_json.py from region_cache (dated copies are
# local baselines kept for comparison)
server/cameras/cameras*.json

# offline build workspace + downloaded MapCreator/extracts
server/offline/.work*/
server/offline/.mc_patch/
server/offline/maps/
